    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "The Philippines won the inaugural Eurovision Song Contest Asia, held in Bangkok, Thailand, with the song \"Sobra-Sobra\" by Carmelle.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-14:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "Voxovation organised the contest under licence from the European Broadcasting Union, with S2O Productions producing and Channel 3 staging it at One Bangkok Forum on 14 November 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385971115:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The Eurovision Song Contest Asia is an international song competition modelled on the Eurovision Song Contest, in which broadcasters from the Asia-Pacific region compete representing their countries.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385971115:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "On 14 November 2026, 71,577 people read the English Wikipedia article, about 28 times the usual daily figure.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Eurovision_Song_Contest_Asia:2026-11-14",
        "views:en:Eurovision_Song_Contest_Asia:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:32Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 11 languages, and after English, the most readers were in Spanish, with 2,451.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Eurovision_Song_Contest_Asia:2026-11-14",
        "views:es:Festival_de_la_Canción_de_Eurovisión_Asia:2026-11-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:39Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers, and a language is not the same as a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:es:Festival_de_la_Canción_de_Eurovisión_Asia:2026-11-14",
        "views:de:Eurovision_Song_Contest_Asia:2026-11-14",
        "views:it:Eurovision_Song_Contest_Asia:2026-11-14",
        "views:fr:Concours_Eurovision_Asie_de_la_chanson:2026-11-14",
        "views:ru:Евровидение_Азия:2026-11-14",
        "views:ja:ユーロビジョン・ソング・コンテスト・アジア:2026-11-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:49Z",
      "text": "The result was reported by AFP and AP.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-14:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:57Z",
      "text": "BBC News headlined its report “Philippines wins first Eurovision Song Contest Asia.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:bbc:3883c6948f3d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:01:03Z",
      "text": "The Guardian headlined its report “Philippines’ Carmelle wins first Eurovision contest in Asia.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:guardian:c629975f6df7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:01:09Z",
      "text": "DW headlined its report “Philippines wins first Eurovision Song Contest Asia.”",
